# How to add your own tutorial

Tutorials are written as plain Doxygen files and typically have the extension dox.


If you prefer to have Python notebooks, please store the notebook (without any 
binary content) in the repo. The notebooks then have to be converted before we 
actually invoke doxygen. This is done by calling

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
python3 documentation/convert-jupyter-notebooks.py
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

If you now call Doxygen, the notebook is integrated into the static webpage.
It will be given the identifier that corresponds to the qualified file path, 
where all / are replaced with underscores.




*/

